3 Key Market Drivers
Structural Health Monitoring: Asset owners are increasingly adopting condition-based monitoring to identify active damage and support predictive maintenance programs.
Aging Industrial Infrastructure: Aging pressure equipment, tanks, pipelines and civil structures are increasing inspection requirements across mature industrial markets.
Remote and Continuous Monitoring: Advances in wireless systems, digital signal processing and remote review are supporting broader deployment beyond traditional inspection projects.

Vertical Industry Watch
Acoustic emission testing is becoming increasingly relevant as industrial operators seek earlier information about structural degradation and equipment integrity. Unlike localized inspection methods, acoustic emission systems can monitor active damage processes while equipment remains under load. This makes the technology valuable for pressure vessels, tanks, pipelines, civil infrastructure and selected renewable-energy assets. Advances in signal processing and digital monitoring are also improving the ability to interpret complex datasets and support remote assessment. As industrial operators move from periodic inspection toward condition-based maintenance, demand for equipment, software and technical services can expand alongside the installed base of aging infrastructure.

